804000-00010</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>Sourceforge.net: Pyrsstep </article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://sourceforge.net/projects/pyrsstep"/></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wood</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Richardson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Wing</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A simple program to create exact person-time data in cohort analyses</article-title><source>Int J Epidemiol</source><year>1997</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>395</fpage><lpage>399</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9169176</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/ije/26.2.395</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Macaluso</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Exact stratification of person-years</article-title><source>Epidemiology</source><year>1992</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>441</fpage><lpage>448</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1391137</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00001648-199209000-00010</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lunn</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>McNeil</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Applying Cox regression to competing risks</article-title><source>Biometrics</source><year>1995</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>524</fpage><lpage>532</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7662841</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/2532940</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nielsen</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>Rostgaard</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Nielsen</surname><given-names>NM</given-names></name><name><surname>Koch-Henriksen</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Haarh</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sorensen</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Hjalgrim</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Multiple sclerosis after infectious mononucleosis</article-title><source>Arch Neurol</source><year>2007</year><volume>64</volume><fpage>72</fpage><lpage>75</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17210811</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/archneur.64.1.72</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shneiderman</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><source>Designing the user interface Strategies for effective human-computer interaction</source><year>1992</year><edition>2</edition><publisher-name>Reading, MA: Addison-Wesley</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>Stata statistical software for professionals</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.stata.com"/></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Data Analysis Products Division, Mathsoft</collab></person-group><source>S-PLUS 2000 Guide to Statistics, Seattle, WA</source><year>1999</year><volume>2</volume></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pearce</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Checkoway</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A simple computer program for generating person-time data in cohort studies involving time-related factors</article-title><source>Am J Epidemiol</source><year>19